@@ -1,6 +1,14 @@
 Release Notes and Change Log
 ============================
 
+1.13.2 (unreleased)
+^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
+* deb: Validate the `Provides` field. Debian policy only allows exact version
+  (`=`) matches in the `Provides` field. fpm now fails at build time, rather
+  than letting `dpkg` fail at install time, when a `--provides` entry uses an
+  invalid version comparison operator (such as `<<`, `<=`, `>=`, `>>`, `<`,
+  `>` or `!=`).
+
 1.13.1 (July 6, 2021)
 ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 * deb: The `--provides` flag now allows for versions. Previously, fpm would
diff --git a/lib/fpm/package/deb.rb b/lib/fpm/package/deb.rb
index 93d9e4d..912f93f 100644
--- a/lib/fpm/package/deb.rb
+++ b/lib/fpm/package/deb.rb
@@ -793,6 +793,23 @@ class FPM::Package::Deb < FPM::Package
       logger.warn("Replacing 'provides' entry #{provides} with syntax 'name (= version)'")
       provides = "#{m[1]} (= #{m[2]})"
     end
+
+    # Debian policy only allows exact version (`=`) matches in the Provides
+    # field. Any other version comparison operator (`<<`, `<=`, `>=`, `>>`,
+    # `<`, `>`, `!=`, etc.) is invalid and will be rejected by dpkg at install
+    # time. Fail at build time so the error is caught early.
+    # See: https://www.debian.org/doc/debian-policy/ch-relationships.html#s7.6
+    if m = provides.match(/\(\s*(\S+)\s+\S/)
+      op = m[1]
+      if op != "="
+        raise FPM::InvalidPackageConfiguration,
+          "Debian policy only allows exact version (`=`) matches in the " \
+          "`Provides` field, but `#{provides}` uses the `#{op}` operator. " \
+          "Only `=` is permitted. See " \
+          "https://www.debian.org/doc/debian-policy/ch-relationships.html#s7.6"
+      end
+    end
+
     return provides.rstrip
   end
 
